  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "Same formula, different compound",
    "kn": "ಒಂದೇ ಸೂತ್ರ, ಬೇರೆ ಸಂಯುಕ್ತ"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "cis-[PtCl₂(NH₃)₂] is the anticancer drug cisplatin; its trans isomer is useless as a drug. Same atoms, different arrangement, very different behaviour.",
    "kn": "cis-[PtCl₂(NH₃)₂] ಕ್ಯಾನ್ಸರ್ ವಿರೋಧಿ ಔಷಧ ಸಿಸ್‌ಪ್ಲಾಟಿನ್; ಅದರ trans ಸಮಾಂಗಿ ಔಷಧವಾಗಿ ಉಪಯೋಗವಿಲ್ಲ. ಅದೇ ಪರಮಾಣುಗಳು, ಬೇರೆ ಜೋಡಣೆ, ಬೇರೆ ಗುಣ."
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "Identify geometrical and optical isomers"
    },
    {
     "en": "Recognise the four types of structural isomerism"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "cis-[PtCl₂(NH₃)₂] is the anticancer drug cisplatin; its trans isomer is useless as a drug. Same atoms, different arrangement, very different behaviour.",
    "kn": "cis-[PtCl₂(NH₃)₂] ಕ್ಯಾನ್ಸರ್ ವಿರೋಧಿ ಔಷಧ ಸಿಸ್‌ಪ್ಲಾಟಿನ್; ಅದರ trans ಸಮಾಂಗಿ ಔಷಧವಾಗಿ ಉಪಯೋಗವಿಲ್ಲ. ಅದೇ ಪರಮಾಣುಗಳು, ಬೇರೆ ಜೋಡಣೆ, ಬೇರೆ ಗುಣ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Stereoisomerism"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Stereoisomers have the same bonds but different arrangements in space. Geometrical isomerism appears in square planar MA₂B₂ (cis and trans) and in octahedral MA₄B₂ and [MX₂(AA)₂] (cis and trans). Octahedral MA₃B₃ gives fac (three like ligands on one face) and mer (around a meridian). Tetrahedral complexes do not show geometrical isomerism. Optical isomers are non-superimposable mirror images (d and l), common in octahedral complexes with didentate ligands: [Co(en)₃]³⁺ and cis-[PtCl₂(en)₂]²⁺ are optically active; the trans form is not.",
    "kn": "ಸ್ಟೀರಿಯೋ ಸಮಾಂಗಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಅದೇ ಬಂಧಗಳು, ಬೇರೆ ಆಕಾಶೀಯ ಜೋಡಣೆ. ಜ್ಯಾಮಿತೀಯ ಸಮಾಂಗತೆ: cis-trans, fac-mer. ಚತುಷ್ಫಲಕೀಯ ಸಂಕೀರ್ಣಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಜ್ಯಾಮಿತೀಯ ಸಮಾಂಗತೆ ಇಲ್ಲ. ದೃಕ್ ಸಮಾಂಗಿಗಳು ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಹೊಂದಿಕೆಯಾಗದ ಕನ್ನಡಿ ಬಿಂಬಗಳು."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Square planar MA₂B₂: cis, trans"
    },
    {
     "en": "Octahedral MA₃B₃: fac, mer"
    },
    {
     "en": "Tetrahedral: no geometrical isomers"
    },
    {
     "en": "Optical: [Co(en)₃]³⁺, cis-[MX₂(AA)₂]"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Stereoisomers have the same bonds but different arrangements in space. Geometrical isomerism appears in square planar MA₂B₂ (cis and trans) and in octahedral MA₄B₂ and [MX₂(AA)₂] (cis and trans). Octahedral MA₃B₃ gives fac (three like ligands on one face) and mer (around a meridian). Tetrahedral complexes do not show geometrical isomerism. Optical isomers are non-superimposable mirror images (d and l), common in octahedral complexes with didentate ligands: [Co(en)₃]³⁺ and cis-[PtCl₂(en)₂]²⁺ are optically active; the trans form is not.",
    "kn": "ಸ್ಟೀರಿಯೋ ಸಮಾಂಗಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಅದೇ ಬಂಧಗಳು, ಬೇರೆ ಆಕಾಶೀಯ ಜೋಡಣೆ. ಜ್ಯಾಮಿತೀಯ ಸಮಾಂಗತೆ: cis-trans, fac-mer. ಚತುಷ್ಫಲಕೀಯ ಸಂಕೀರ್ಣಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಜ್ಯಾಮಿತೀಯ ಸಮಾಂಗತೆ ಇಲ್ಲ. ದೃಕ್ ಸಮಾಂಗಿಗಳು ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಹೊಂದಿಕೆಯಾಗದ ಕನ್ನಡಿ ಬಿಂಬಗಳು."
   }
