  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Structural isomerism"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Structural isomers have different bonds. Linkage isomerism: an ambidentate ligand binds through different atoms, e.g. [Co(NH₃)₅(NO₂)]Cl₂ (yellow, N-bound) and [Co(NH₃)₅(ONO)]Cl₂ (red, O-bound). Coordination isomerism: ligands are exchanged between a complex cation and a complex anion, e.g. [Co(NH₃)₆][Cr(CN)₆] and [Cr(NH₃)₆][Co(CN)₆]. Ionisation isomerism: a counter ion swaps with a ligand, e.g. [Co(NH₃)₅(SO₄)]Br and [Co(NH₃)₅Br]SO₄. Solvate (hydrate) isomerism: water inside or outside the sphere, e.g. [Cr(H₂O)₆]Cl₃ (violet) and [Cr(H₂O)₅Cl]Cl₂·H₂O (grey-green).",
    "kn": "ರಚನಾ ಸಮಾಂಗಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಬಂಧಗಳೇ ಬೇರೆ: ಬಂಧನ, ಸಮನ್ವಯ, ಅಯಾನೀಕರಣ ಮತ್ತು ದ್ರಾವಕ (ಜಲ) ಸಮಾಂಗತೆ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Linkage: NO₂⁻/ONO⁻, SCN⁻/NCS⁻"
    },
    {
     "en": "Coordination: swap between cation and anion complexes"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ionisation: different ions in solution"
    },
    {
     "en": "Hydrate: [Cr(H₂O)₆]Cl₃ isomers"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Structural isomers have different bonds. Linkage isomerism: an ambidentate ligand binds through different atoms, e.g. [Co(NH₃)₅(NO₂)]Cl₂ (yellow, N-bound) and [Co(NH₃)₅(ONO)]Cl₂ (red, O-bound). Coordination isomerism: ligands are exchanged between a complex cation and a complex anion, e.g. [Co(NH₃)₆][Cr(CN)₆] and [Cr(NH₃)₆][Co(CN)₆]. Ionisation isomerism: a counter ion swaps with a ligand, e.g. [Co(NH₃)₅(SO₄)]Br and [Co(NH₃)₅Br]SO₄. Solvate (hydrate) isomerism: water inside or outside the sphere, e.g. [Cr(H₂O)₆]Cl₃ (violet) and [Cr(H₂O)₅Cl]Cl₂·H₂O (grey-green).",
    "kn": "ರಚನಾ ಸಮಾಂಗಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಬಂಧಗಳೇ ಬೇರೆ: ಬಂಧನ, ಸಮನ್ವಯ, ಅಯಾನೀಕರಣ ಮತ್ತು ದ್ರಾವಕ (ಜಲ) ಸಮಾಂಗತೆ."
   }
  },
